meta {
  name: availability
  type: folder
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Availability calendar + CRUD. Center-scoped under /centers/{{center_id}}/availability/.

  Folders (test order):
  1. operating-hours — set weekly clinic hours (PATCH then GET)
  2. closures — close/reopen dates
  3. calendars — read computed availability (start=YYYY-MM-DD)
  4. associates — roster / blocks / leaves
  5. rooms — blocks / downtimes
  6. equipment — blocks / downtimes

  Aggregate associate calendar lives under bruno/associates/ (not center-scoped).

  All writes use {detail, data}. Block POSTs (assoc/room/equip): data = array of created rows; use data[0].id / data[n].id for env ids.
  Writes that trigger exception detection may also return top-level exception_scan: queued | completed | resolved | skipped (data shape unchanged).
  Async scans (recurring blocks, roster): run `uv run manage.py process_appointment_exception_scans` (~1 min cron).

  Sample fixtures clustered early Sep 2026 so calendar GETs see CRUD seed data.

  Center calendar GET defaults granularity=week; other calendars default day.
  Associates: X-Center-ID must match center_id.
  Env: center_id, associate_id, room_id, equipment_id, closure_id,
  associate_block_id, associate_leave_id, room_block_id, room_downtime_id,
  equipment_block_id, equipment_downtime_id.
}
